I disagree. Even with non-permanent footrice corpses you won't make a
single move in unknown territory[*]; that won't change if the corpse
becomes non-rotting. The same for foocubus encounters. (And not much
different WRT accidental eating the corpse; you'll have it in a bag
anyway and just take it out temporarily to fight _while not moving_.)

(I agree that if you have a permanent corpse in your possension the
statistics would evolve to the worse; but counting on inattentiveness
is a different point compared to the "balance of game features". And
we really don't need another factor of the "GUI design trap". IMO.)

